<article class="env-definition" id="03YK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03YK">Definition <span data-tag="03YK">94.10.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme contained in $\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$. Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a $1$-morphism of categories fibred in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. Assume $f$ is representable by algebraic spaces. Let $\mathcal{P}$ be a property of morphisms of algebraic spaces which </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
is preserved under any base change, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
is fppf local on the base, see Descent on Spaces, Definition <a href="/tag/03YH" data-tag="03YH">74.10.1</a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> In this case we say that $f$ has <em>property $\mathcal{P}$</em> if for every $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits ((\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf})$ and any $y \in \mathcal{Y}_ U$ the resulting morphism of algebraic spaces $f_ y : F_ y \to U$, see diagram (<a href="/tag/0402" data-tag="0402">94.9.1.1</a>), has property $\mathcal{P}$. </p>
</article>